{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "new `tautline fleet-lease` verb claims/renews/releases/takes over cross-worktree working-set leases stored in <git-common-dir>/tautline-fleet/",
    "new `fleet-guard-hook` PreToolUse guard blocks edits to paths leased by another lane, with three runnable escapes; enforcement is per the new adapter `fleet` domain (block default, or advise/observe)",
    "methodology-status --fail-on-drift counts fleet-guard-hook as a required hook; recover with `tautline install-hooks` or any lane-start",
    "repos with no leases are unaffected: the guard short-circuits before any lease parsing, so single-lane checkouts see no new friction",
    "guard scope is the structured file-edit tools (Edit/Write/MultiEdit/NotebookEdit); writes issued through Bash are NOT guarded in v1",
    "lease glob syntax is *, ? and ** only; bracket classes match literally"
  ],
